# Health Knowledge Assistant

A web app where users sign up, upload public health documents (PDF), and ask
questions. An AI answers using only those documents and cites the pages it used.

![Chat screenshot](docs/chat.png)

## Features
- Signup and login with JWT authentication and Argon2 password hashing
- PDF upload, text extraction, chunking, and embeddings stored in PostgreSQL (pgvector)
- Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG): answers come only from retrieved passages, with page citations
- Relevance cutoff: unrelated questions get "I could not find this" instead of a guess
- Per-user document isolation and ownership checks on delete
- Retry with backoff when the LLM API is temporarily unavailable

## Architecture
Browser (Next.js) -> FastAPI -> PostgreSQL + pgvector
                         |
                         +-> Gemini API (embeddings and answers)

## Tech stack
Next.js, React, TypeScript, Tailwind | FastAPI, Python, SQLAlchemy, Pydantic |
PostgreSQL + pgvector | Gemini API | Docker Compose | GitHub Actions | pytest

## Run it locally
1. Copy `backend/.env.example` to `backend/.env` and fill in your values
2. `docker compose up --build`
3. Open http://localhost:3001

## Privacy
Use only public documents or synthetic data. Never upload real patient data.

## Testing
`cd backend && pytest` (also runs in GitHub Actions on every push)

